---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import quickstartSrc from "../../examples/quickstart.rs?raw";
import programSrc from "../../examples/first-machine.sst?raw";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---
<Base title="Quick Start" current="quickstart">
  <article class="shell narrow guide-body">
    <h1>Quick Start</h1>
    <p>
      Build a machine that adds two numbers and returns 42. It declares an
      arithmetic dialect, implements a calculator component, and connects it to
      program execution through an authored composite.
    </p>
    <p>
      Begin with the <a href={`${base}/guide`}>version and dependency setup</a>,
      then save the SST program as <code>src/first-machine.sst</code> and the Rust
      code as <code>src/main.rs</code>. Run <code>cargo run</code>. The
      <a href={`${base}/guide/first-machine`}>first machine walkthrough</a>
      explains each part.
    </p>
    <h2>The SST program</h2>
    <pre><code>{programSrc}</code></pre>
    <h2>The Rust machine</h2>
    <pre><code class="language-rust">{quickstartSrc}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Continue through the <a href={`${base}/guide/mental-model`}>mental model</a>
      and <a href={`${base}/guide`}>author’s guide</a>, or look up individual
      types in the <a href={`${base}/reference`}>API reference</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
